==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/əˈstɪɡmətɪzm̩/|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
From {{prefix|a||t1=not|lang=en}} stem of {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|lang=grc|στίγμα||tr=stigma|mark, point}} {{suffix||ism|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{context|optics|lang=en}} A defect of a [[lens]] such that light rays coming from a point do not meet at a [[focal point]] so that the image is blurred.
# {{context|pathology|lang=en}} A disorder of the vision, usually due to a misshapen [[cornea]], such that light does not focus correctly on the [[retina]] causing a blurred image.

====Synonyms====
* [[astigmia]]

====Derived terms====
* [[astigmatic]]
* [[astigmatically]]

====Related terms====
* [[stigma]]
* [[stigmatize]]

